<section class="cp-topic" id="coverage">
<h2>Topic coverage</h2>
<p>This tool covers the same 27 California counties covered in <a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/digitalcoast/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA's</a> <a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/digitalcoast/tools/snapshots.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coastal County Snapshots</a> tool. As with that tool, 23 counties come from the original <a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/digitalcoast/data/enow.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Economics: National Ocean Watch (ENOW)</a> dataset, which <a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/data/digitalcoast/pdf/enow-faq.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">expands on NOAA's definition</a> of <a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/data/digitalcoast/pdf/qrt-coastal-county-definitions.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"coastal shoreline counties"</a> by dropping "shore-adjacent counties with no relevant economic activity" and adding inland ones with "significant levels of ocean- and Great Lakes-dependent economic activity". Four counties were added because <a href="https://www.fema.gov/flood-maps/national-flood-hazard-layer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA flood data</a> is available. Additional <a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/slr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">sea level rise data</a> was used to add Sea Level Rise topics to the three delta counties.</p>

