<section class="cp-topic" id="gauges">
<h2>Sea Level Rise Guidance</h2>
<p>This tool follows the published <a href="https://opc.ca.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ocean Protection Council (OPC)</a> <a href="https://opc.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/California-Sea-Level-Rise-Guidance-2024-508.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2024 California Sea Level Rise Guidance</a>. As per the guidance (pp. 7-8), this tool includes the Intermediate, Intermediate-High, and High scenarios relative to a year 2000 baseline. Broadly speaking, at a "High" scenario at the 2050 and 2100 years in the OPC guidance, the state on average will see 1.2 feet and 6.6 feet respectively of sea level rise. However, the average sea level rise hits 2.0 feet at the "High" scenario in 2060, so I feel a 2 foot minimum matching the NOAA Coastal County Snapshots is still relevant as a "near term (2020-2050)" planning tool, especially considering combined impacts such as El Niño impacts and storm events (for more on this, see "Combined Impacts of Sea Level Rise and Other Coastal Hazards" on pp. 38-52).</p>

<p>"Average" doesn't paint the county-level picture; as the OPC guidance states, local site conditions will impact the specific sea level scenario at each tide gauge (p. 55). The tide-gauge-specific sea level rise scenarios in Appendix 2 (pp. 85-92) were used for Sea Level Rise topics in this tool; simple linear interpolation was used between decades to determine year-specific height projections. To simplify the tool, I made an editorial decision to pick one tide gauge per county; some were "obvious" and had a nearby gauge, while others were judgement calls based on what I thought was relevant to the selected county. The county profile and the linked gauges are listed below. For project planning, OPC guidance suggests either finding the nearest tide gauge, or to average two if equidistant (p. 56). Tide gauge locations along with heights at specific scenarios and years are visible as a layer on the <a href="{{ '/map/#map=6%2F37.20000%2F-119.40000&base=Greyscale&on=id%3AcountyToggle%2Cid%3AnasaSlrToggle&v=id%3AnasaSlrScenario%7EInt%7Cid%3AnasaSlrYear%7E2050' | url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CASCA Map tool</a>CASCA Map tool</a>.</p>
