<section class="cp-topic" id="limits">
<h2>Limitations</h2>
<section class="cp-topic" id="vulnerabilities">
<h3>Business vulnerability data unavailable</h3>
<p>NOAA's snapshots used Esri Business Analyst 2019 data to map vulnerable businesses situated on the 100-year floodplain and exposed to 6 feet of Sea Level Rise. Unfortunately, that data set is licensed and can't be recreated using public data; as a result, business exposure is missing from all topics. For Sea Level Rise, Total Economy, and Flood Hazard topics, exposed jobs are used instead, calculated from LODES workplace data mapped out in the risk areas. LODES data is not granular enough at the marine sector level to be used as a replacement for Marine Economy business risks, so it is omitted entirely.</p>
</section>
<section class="cp-topic" id="differences-from-enow">
<h3>Differences from NOAA's published ENOW</h3>
<p>As mentioned, this tool uses a generated data set based on the ENOW methodology in lieu of an updated ENOW dataset. Read more at <a href="{{ '/county-profiles/about/economy/' | url }}">Economy figures in detail</a>.</p>
</section>
</section>